# Original analytic-to-translated two-layer graph route

This is a pure source/interface plan. No candidate is kernel-validated or published.

Exact chain: `OAI.PiExponent.LiteralAnalytic.actual_minor_analytic_bound` → `OAI.PiExponent.LiteralAnalytic.norm_actual_summand_le` → `OAI.PiExponent.DeterminantAnalyticBound.translated_summand_bound`.

The last child is genuinely Accepted: theorem `4340823c-de0b-446e-9161-c7ddd0bcb17a`, proof `6f3fb375-a5ab-4052-a59d-90a06cba315e`.
The outer source proof also reuses genuinely Accepted `log_norm_sum_le`; it does not recreate that theorem.

Literal Published31/structure-owner coverage leaves exactly **17 original data commands, 49 lines** needed to state the direct child interfaces. They contain no theorem commands.

Prepare that one data package first; then publish missing exact original-type Open children and submit the two original proof suffixes as sketches. This creates the two requested graph links before closing every analytic sibling.

