All full statements, scopes, original commands, source/port hashes and source commit are saved in `report.json`, `source-units/` and `original-source-units/`. Both parent proof suffixes are literally original; two future child proofs have existing finite port differences: `card_choiceFamily_le` uses `Finset.prod_le_prod` → `Finset.prod_le_prod'`, and `norm_scalar_product_le` uses `Finset.prod_le_prod₀` → `Finset.prod_le_prod`. These are explicitly recorded and are not falsely labeled unchanged original proofs.

Candidate imports use Mathlib and actual platform Definitions/Theorems paths; the 17-Def module is explicitly pending. No original-source OAI import or global solution is used as a dependency.

The 31 recorded Definition readbacks and both Accepted theorem records are pinned directly; mutable progress is used only to select this frozen snapshot and is not an input pin. Final compilers must establish actual ownership, full Def values, imported OLeans, source/generated complete types/refs, Std3 and expected Open sorryAx. Raw owned CI inventories must precede any automatic-helper classification.
